Exactly.  The only reason for gaining levels is either to get the
additional skill slots, or to get more hit points, and you can get the
latter more effectively through alchemy.

(Okay, actually there's at least one more possible reason to gain levels
that I can think of, which is that various classes/races get intrinsics at
particular experience levels, but I don't think any intrinsics are gained
by any race or class after level 20.  And even these cases are unlikely to
be useful; tourists gain poison resistance at level 20, and priest(esse)s
gain fire resistance at level 20, but it's unlikely that either class won't
have these by this point.)

